;; M, the Last Step: the payoff. The stone's root ends here over the floor;
;; the bearers' story runs along the back wall. The way back is the old air
;; shaft (columns 22-23, steady ^, enclosed), entered at its foot (column
;; 21, rows 8-9): it rises through J into I and only ever goes up.
(room
  region: underhum
  at: (8 7)
  title: "The Last Step"
  intent: "the bottom of the cistern, where the stone's root ends and the bearers' story is cut into the wall"
  bed: (hum 0.9 air 0.5 water 0)
  light: 0.2
  grid:
  ("######################^^#"
   "######################^^#"
   "######################^^#"
   "#                    #^^#"
   "#                    #^^#"
   "#                    #^^#"
   "#                    #^^#"
   "#                    #^^#"
   "                      ^^#"
   "                      ^^#"
   "#########################")
  things: ((root at: (17 3))
           (mural at: (2 6) image: bearers-story))
  decor: none)
